{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Client-visible divergence now reproduces too (A's FSM keeps six applied commands, B's five, after A's committed entry is truncated). Submitting the extended successor."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_dual_majority_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"dd5cdfe7274a4444b305c5d104f6e5c8-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":(\\\"The executed revision established the silent change and the truncation of the committed entry. This revision adds the client-facing observation of the same path: a client write issued on the {A,B,E} leader A after the silent change (committed with A and E) and the FSM contents of A and of the old-majority leader afterwards. It also drops the earlier 'at most one leader' comparison because a construction-time run of this revision observed A stepping down before the old side's leader was sampled (vote requests in the higher term reach A from the connected side), so the leader-concurrency window is schedule-dependent and is retained as an observation from the two scored executions rather than as a comparison in this harness.\\\"),\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"truncate_conflict\\\",\\\"cfg_change_gate\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Four in-process nodes at protocol version 3 with 300ms heartbeat/election/lease: A and B bootstrapped as voters {A,B}; A snapshots, adds E as a caught-up nonvoter, adds C as a voter, commits four commands. A is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs=true so its configuration comes from the snapshot ({A,B}) while its log holds {A,B,C}; B is partitioned; A issues AddVoter E, which the stale base turns into the two-server change {A,B,E} and which commits on A plus E. The probe then issues one client command on A (committed with A and E) and finally heals the partition, observing the entry at the created index and the FSM contents of A and of the old-majority leader.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"E is a caught-up nonvoter before the change, so {A,B,E} commits with A and E alone once B is partitioned.\\\",\\\"The client command is an ordinary Apply on the leader that has a quorum of the configuration recorded in its own log ({A,B,E}: A and E).\\\",\\\"MockFSM records one entry per LogCommand applied, so its length is the number of committed commands that node's FSM has consumed.\\\",\\\"Both sides keep running the protocol; the partition is applied by disconnecting in-memory transports in both directions.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No control variant: with the flag disabled the configuration is current, so the same AddVoter is a single-server change and cannot create the disjoint majorities (nextConfiguration over the current configuration).\\\",\\\"Leader concurrency is not asserted as a comparison here because its window depends on when the higher-term vote requests reach the stale leader.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"nodes\\\":4,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"leader_lease_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"other_side_election_timeout_ms\\\":3000}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real snapshot, real AddNonvoter catch-up, real AddVoter, real commits, graceful shutdown and restart of the leader on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances, real client Apply, real transport partition and real healing. Nothing is fabricated.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation2\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"silent_change\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_type_at_x\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"LogConfiguration\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_fsm\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"client_write\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation2\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed_entry_truncated\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry committed under the configuration recorded in the logs must not be replaced after the partition heals.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_fsm\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"fsm_logs_equal\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After a client write returns success on the leader, every node that follows the same log must apply the same committed commands; the FSMs of A and of the old-majority leader must not differ.\\\"}\n ]\n}\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['limitations']=[l for l in i['limitations'] if 'repeat' not in l and 'superseded receipt' not in l]\ni['limitations'] += [\n \\\"Leader concurrency on the two sides was observed in the two scored executions (A still leader in term 3 while B led term 4) but a later construction-time run of the extended harness observed A already stepped down when the old side's leader was sampled, so that window is schedule-dependent; the reproducible consequences are the truncation of the committed entry and the resulting FSM divergence.\\\",\n \\\"The extended harness adds the client write and FSM observations; its retained receipt is requested in this update, so the FSM-divergence comparison is claimed from the construction-time run plus source (appendEntries clears the conflicting suffix, and lastApplied only moves forward, state.go 136-141) until that receipt exists.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_dual_majority_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"dd5cdfe7274a4444b305c5d104f6e5c8-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":(\\\"The executed revision established the silent change and the truncation of the committed entry. This revision adds the client-facing observation of the same path: a client write issued on the {A,B,E} leader A after the silent change (committed with A and E) and the FSM contents of A and of the old-majority leader afterwards. It also drops the earlier 'at most one leader' comparison because a construction-time run of this revision observed A stepping down before the old side's leader was sampled (vote requests in the higher term reach A from the connected side), so the leader-concurrency window is schedule-dependent and is retained as an observation from the two scored executions rather than as a comparison in this harness.\\\"),\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"truncate_conflict\\\",\\\"cfg_change_gate\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Four in-process nodes at protocol version 3 with 300ms heartbeat/election/lease: A and B bootstrapped as voters {A,B}; A snapshots, adds E as a caught-up nonvoter, adds C as a voter, commits four commands. A is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs=true so its configuration comes from the snapshot ({A,B}) while its log holds {A,B,C}; B is partitioned; A issues AddVoter E, which the stale base turns into the two-server change {A,B,E} and which commits on A plus E. The probe then issues one client command on A (committed with A and E) and finally heals the partition, observing the entry at the created index and the FSM contents of A and of the old-majority leader.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"E is a caught-up nonvoter before the change, so {A,B,E} commits with A and E alone once B is partitioned.\\\",\\\"The client command is an ordinary Apply on the leader that has a quorum of the configuration recorded in its own log ({A,B,E}: A and E).\\\",\\\"MockFSM records one entry per LogCommand applied, so its length is the number of committed commands that node's FSM has consumed.\\\",\\\"Both sides keep running the protocol; the partition is applied by disconnecting in-memory transports in both directions.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No control variant: with the flag disabled the configuration is current, so the same AddVoter is a single-server change and cannot create the disjoint majorities (nextConfiguration over the current configuration).\\\",\\\"Leader concurrency is not asserted as a comparison here because its window depends on when the higher-term vote requests reach the stale leader.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"nodes\\\":4,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"leader_lease_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"other_side_election_timeout_ms\\\":3000}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real snapshot, real AddNonvoter catch-up, real AddVoter, real commits, graceful shutdown and restart of the leader on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances, real client Apply, real transport partition and real healing. Nothing is fabricated.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation2\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"silent_change\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_type_at_x\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"LogConfiguration\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_fsm\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"client_write\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation2\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed_entry_truncated\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry committed under the configuration recorded in the logs must not be replaced after the partition heals.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_fsm\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"fsm_logs_equal\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After a client write returns success on the leader, every node that follows the same log must apply the same committed commands; the FSMs of A and of the old-majority leader must not differ.\\\"}\n ]\n}\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['limitations']=[l for l in i['limitations'] if 'repeat' not in l and 'superseded receipt' not in l]\ni['limitations'] += [\n \\\"Leader concurrency on the two sides was observed in the two scored executions (A still leader in term 3 while B led term 4) but a later construction-time run of the extended harness observed A already stepped down when the old side's leader was sampled, so that window is schedule-dependent; the reproducible consequences are the truncation of the committed entry and the resulting FSM divergence.\\\",\n \\\"The extended harness adds the client write and FSM observations; its retained receipt is requested in this update, so the FSM-divergence comparison is claimed from the construction-time run plus source (appendEntries clears the conflicting suffix, and lastApplied only moves forward, state.go 136-141) until that receipt exists.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open